course: dictionary
lesson: 3740
title: Floss: one word, three meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. You can find the right one by reading the words around it. «Use dental floss to clean between your teeth.» Here, the words teeth and clean tell you that floss is a thin thread for cleaning. Always check the clues first.
explain: «Floss is slid gently between the teeth and curved around each tooth.» Gently and curved show you how to use the thread: softly, and around each tooth. The word floss can also be a verb. «Dentists say you should floss once a day» means to clean between your teeth with thread.
explain: Some words are much more fun. «We bought candy floss at the fair.» The words candy and fair give the clue: it is a fluffy pink sweet. The word floss can even be a dance. «Do the floss» means swinging your arms and hips from side to side. When you meet floss, ask: does the sentence talk about teeth, sweets or dancing?
fact: Dental floss is a thin thread used to clean between your teeth.
fact: To floss means to clean between your teeth with a thread.
fact: A toothbrush cannot reach the narrow gaps between the teeth, so floss helps clean there.
fact: Candy floss (British) is a fluffy pink sweet made of spun sugar; Americans call it cotton candy.
fact: The floss is also a dance where you swing your arms and hips from side to side.
exercise: «Use dental floss to clean between your teeth.» What is dental floss? | A pink sweet sold at the fair | A small tube of toothpaste | A soft brush for cleaning your tongue | *A thin thread for cleaning between your teeth
exercise: «A toothbrush cannot reach the narrow gaps between the teeth, so we use floss.» Where can floss reach that a brush cannot? | On the lips | On the top of the tongue | *Between the teeth | Inside the cheeks only
exercise: Ella says, «Let's do the floss at the party!» What is the floss here? | *A swinging dance move | A way of brushing your teeth twice | A fluffy pink sweet | A visit to the dentist
test: «We bought candy floss at the fair.» What is candy floss? | *A fluffy pink sweet made of spun sugar | A type of soft towel | A thin thread for cleaning teeth | A sort of bread roll
test: Why do dentists tell us to floss? | To make your breath smell of sugar | To stop yourself from ever needing a brush | *To clean the gaps between teeth where a brush cannot reach | To paint your teeth a whiter colour
exam: «Dentists say you should floss once a day.» In this sentence, what kind of word is floss? | pronoun | adjective | *verb | noun
